The function `mptcp_pm_nl_flush_addrs_doit()` in this commit still uses the non-RCU-safe `list_splice_init()` on `pernet->endp_list` (renamed from `local_addr_list` in this commit) as shown in lines 1199-1202: 

	spin_lock_bh(&pernet->lock);
	list_splice_init(&pernet->endp_list, &free_list);

This allows concurrent RCU readers traversing `pernet->endp_list` (e.g., in `select_local_address` or `select_signal_address`) to encounter a corrupted list state, leading to potential crashes.
